	(text "GPS + Qwiic: GPS port (J802) with its supply choice and ESD protection, PPS pad, Qwiic I2C port (J803)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "83b45be0-272a-5808-8a24-492c08e86770")
	)
	(text_box "WHAT IT DOES\nJ802 takes a GPS module (JST GH 6-pin, Pixhawk pinout). Its serial port (UART) goes to the ESP32 through 100R resistors, its\nI2C pins (GPS compass) join the board's I2C bus, and U802 protects the two UART lines from static discharge at the connector.\nJP801 picks the GPS supply: 3.3 V as delivered (pads 1-2 bridged), or 5 V through F803 (cut 1-2, bridge 2-3) for 5 V GPS units.\nThe GPS shares ESP32 UART2 with the RS232 port, so only one of the two works at a time. TP801 is the GPS PPS (time pulse) pad.\nJ803 is a Qwiic port for more I2C sensors. Net labels with the same name on this sheet are connected (e.g. GPS_TX_EXT).\n\nPINS OF THIS MODULE (its block on the top sheet)\n+3V3 (in): GPS supply (default) and the Qwiic port\n+5V (in): GPS 5 V option (through F803) and the reference of U802\nGPS_RXD (in): from ESP32 GPIO16 (UART2 TX) to the GPS's RX, J802 pin 2\nGPS_TXD (out): from the GPS's TX, J802 pin 3, to ESP32 GPIO17 (UART2 RX)\nGPS_PPS (out): GPS time pulse from TP801 to ESP32 GPIO4\nI2C_SCL, I2C_SDA (both ways): the shared I2C bus: J802 pins 4/5, J803 pins 4/3\nGND: ground\nPower and ground reach the parts on this sheet only through these pins: the ground and supply symbols drawn on this sheet are local to it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 17.78 0)
		(size 388 36.8)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dde245c2-8886-5e9b-bd77-0ad02975d4df")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 66.04 116.84)
		(end 172.72 200.66)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type dash)
			(color 200 60 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(uuid "48481871-d08e-5d92-9e28-d0b4d01f0653")
	)
	(text "GPS port: keep these at J802"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 66.64 117.44 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.0 1.0)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "88ec732a-ecf9-5698-b8ab-ffac2b14a7a4")
	)
	(text "U802 (ESD diodes), R803 and R804 sit right at J802: after the connector,\nthe UART lines meet the ESD diodes first, with a short GND path.\nC802 belongs to U802 pin 5 (VP): within 2 mm, GND via beside its GND pad."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 175.26 152.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(color 200 60 0 1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "58e49840-980d-51ec-9850-09b90806e36a")
	)
	(text_box "PARTS AND THEIR JOBS\nJ802: GPS port, JST GH 6-pin, Pixhawk pinout: 1 VCC, 2 TX to the GPS's RX, 3 RX from the GPS's TX, 4 SCL, 5 SDA, 6 GND. 3.3 V logic, not 5 V-tolerant.\nJP801: 3-pad solder jumper for the GPS supply (GPS_VCC): pads 1-2 bridged = 3.3 V as delivered; cut 1-2 and bridge 2-3 for a 5 V GPS.\nF803: 0.2 A resettable fuse (trips at 0.46 A): protects +5V when the GPS runs from 5 V.\nR804, R803: 100R in series with the line to the GPS's RX and from its TX: they limit the current into a wrong or unpowered device.\nR806: 100k pull-up: holds GPS_TXD (the ESP32's RX input) high when no GPS is plugged in.\nU802: SRV05-4 ESD protection diodes on the two UART lines at J802 (its other two channels are unused); VP on +5V, VN on GND.\nC802: 100 nF decoupling for U802 VP (pin 5).\nTP801, R805, R807: TP801 is the PPS solder pad (GPS time pulse); R805 100R in series to GPIO4; R807 100k holds GPS_PPS low when nothing is connected.\nJ803: Qwiic port, JST SH 4-pin: 1 GND, 2 3.3 V (not fused: keep external devices under 50 mA), 3 SDA, 4 SCL. Also takes a u-blox GPS over I2C (0x42).\nTP807, TP808: Probe pads for +3V3 and GND.\nGPS_VCC, GPS_5V, GPS_RX_EXT, GPS_TX_EXT, GPS_PPS_EXT: Net labels: the connector side of each line. The same name means the same net."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 231 0)
		(size 280 28.6)
		(margins 1.5 1.5 1.5 1.5)
		(stroke
			(width 0.1524)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
